{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And charge Yehoshua.</b> Regarding the burdens and the loads and the disputes." "<b>And strengthen him and encourage him.</b> With your words — that his heart not grow weak, saying: Just as my master was punished on their account, so too will I end up punished on their account. I assure him that he will cross over and he will bring them to inherit (see Sifrei)." "<b>For he will cross.</b> If he crosses before them they will inherit, and if not, they will not inherit. And so you find: when he sent from the people to Ai and he sat, ״וַיַּכּוּ מֵהֶם אַנְשֵׁי הָעַי״ (Joshua 7) — and since he fell on his face, He said to him: ״קוּם לָךְ״ — <b>קָם לָךְ</b> is written: you are the one standing in your place and sending my children to war — why are you falling on your face? Did I not say to Moshe your master: if he crosses, they cross, and if not, they do not cross? (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:53.132892014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}